\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The left panel illustrates the plaqeutte configurations $\mathfrak  {P}$ and $\mathfrak  {S}$ as well as the edge configuration $\mathfrak  {D}_Z$. The set of plaquettes in pink is denoted by $\mathfrak  {P}$, while the set containing those in pink-blue is denoted by $\mathfrak  {S}$. The edge configuration $\mathfrak  {D}_Z$ consists of all of the red $z$-directional edges in the system, as shown in the above figure. The right panel illustrates the zigzag configuration $\mathfrak  {D}_{zz}$ consisting of edges at all the horizontal loops. Such an edge configuration is also the boundary of both $\mathfrak  {P}$ and $\mathfrak  {S}$, for which we can write $\mathfrak  {D}_{zz} = \partial \mathfrak  {P} = \partial \mathfrak  {S}$. Note that $\Sigma _{\mathfrak  {D}_Z}=\Sigma _{\mathfrak  {D}_{zz}}$ although $\mathrm  {EP}(\mathfrak  {D}_Z)\neq  \mathrm  {EP}(\mathfrak  {D}_{zz})=\varnothing $}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig.S-P-dimer-gas}{{2}{5}{The left panel illustrates the plaqeutte configurations $\mathfrak {P}$ and $\mathfrak {S}$ as well as the edge configuration $\mathfrak {D}_Z$. The set of plaquettes in pink is denoted by $\mathfrak {P}$, while the set containing those in pink-blue is denoted by $\mathfrak {S}$. The edge configuration $\mathfrak {D}_Z$ consists of all of the red $z$-directional edges in the system, as shown in the above figure. The right panel illustrates the zigzag configuration $\mathfrak {D}_{zz}$ consisting of edges at all the horizontal loops. Such an edge configuration is also the boundary of both $\mathfrak {P}$ and $\mathfrak {S}$, for which we can write $\mathfrak {D}_{zz} = \de \mathfrak {P} = \de \mathfrak {S}$. Note that $\Sigma _{\mathfrak {D}_Z}=\Sigma _{\mathfrak {D}_{zz}}$ although $\mrm {EP}(\mathfrak {D}_Z)\neq \mrm {EP}(\mathfrak {D}_{zz})=\varnothing $}{figure.2}{}}
