\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces $\mathfrak  {D}_1$ and $\mathfrak  {D}_2$ are equivalent configurations because they share the same set of endpoints. $\mathfrak  {D}_2$ can be decomposed into two strings ($\overline  {i_1i_2}$ and $\overline  {i_3i_4}$) that connect different types of endpoints, while $\mathfrak  {D}_1$ is composed of two strings ($\overline  {i_1i_3}$ and $\overline  {i_2i_4}$) connecting the same type of endpoints. Another configuration $\mathfrak  {D}_3$ is the combination of two strings ($\overline  {i_1i_4}$ and $\overline  {i_2i_3}$) connecting different types of endpoints. Still, the intersection part (brown dotted segment $\overline  {ab}$ at the center of the figure) vanishes because the combination is accomplished by performing $\oplus $ between the two edge configurations, making it equivalent to the combination of two strings $\overline  {i_1i_3}$ and $\overline  {i_2i_4}$ with the order of $i_3$ and $i_4$ being swapped. }}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig.standard-configuration}{{3}{7}{$\mathfrak {D}_1$ and $\mathfrak {D}_2$ are equivalent configurations because they share the same set of endpoints. $\mathfrak {D}_2$ can be decomposed into two strings ($\overline {i_1i_2}$ and $\overline {i_3i_4}$) that connect different types of endpoints, while $\mathfrak {D}_1$ is composed of two strings ($\overline {i_1i_3}$ and $\overline {i_2i_4}$) connecting the same type of endpoints. Another configuration $\mathfrak {D}_3$ is the combination of two strings ($\overline {i_1i_4}$ and $\overline {i_2i_3}$) connecting different types of endpoints. Still, the intersection part (brown dotted segment $\overline {ab}$ at the center of the figure) vanishes because the combination is accomplished by performing $\oplus $ between the two edge configurations, making it equivalent to the combination of two strings $\overline {i_1i_3}$ and $\overline {i_2i_4}$ with the order of $i_3$ and $i_4$ being swapped}{figure.3}{}}
